  "id": "COMPOUND:14494 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "N-methylscopolamine is proposed to interact with MOVP-3 through a multi-step mechanism involving the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is targeted by both N-methylscopolamine and other compounds, such as (+)-Menthol and (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-(Hydroxymethyl)-6-[3-[(E)-3-Hydroxyprop-1-Enyl]-2,5-Dimethoxyphenoxy]Oxane-3,4,5-Triol, which in turn target MOVP-3. The presence of multiple pathways converging on MOVP-3 suggests a potential role for the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 in mediating the interaction between N-methylscopolamine and MOVP-3. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where N-methylscopolamine may inhibit MOVP-3 by modulating the activity of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, potentially through a direct or indirect interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 acting as a central mediator in the observed effects. The evidence is consistent with a biologically plausible mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
